Package: martinmunk-avr-controld
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3.13
Description: broker daemon for AV receivers (serial/telnet), socket API, MQTT
 avr-controld owns the one connection to an AV receiver (NAD, Opalum, ...) and
 serves it to the ALSA volume plugins, the HDMI-CEC relay and an AirPlay power
 policy over a Unix socket, and optionally to Home Assistant as MQTT entities
 (power/volume/mute/input and every extra the receiver exposes). It ships a
 self-contained virtualenv under /opt/avr-controld/venv with all Python
 dependencies bundled (nad_receiver, paho-mqtt, pyserial), so nothing is pulled
 from PyPI on the target and everything stays dpkg-tracked.
